A copy of part of R's math library (nmath), for builds of dbarts that do not
run inside R. The R package never compiles it: there the engine calls R's own
routines. .Rbuildignore keeps the whole standalone/ directory out of the
package tarball.

Source
------

R 4.6.2, src/nmath, from the CRAN release tarball
https://cran.r-project.org/src/base/R-4/R-4.6.2.tar.gz
(SHA-256 c297040f6392b1dac6e5c0eb398422cfdaedf540ae2205edb9ad0d10cb10ee00).

Copied unedited, the closure of the six routines dbarts calls (pnorm, qnorm,
dnorm, dt, qt, qchisq) and nothing else:

  bd0.c chebyshev.c cospi.c d1mach.c dgamma.c dnorm.c dpois.c dt.c fmax2.c
  fmin2.c gamma.c i1mach.c lbeta.c lgamma.c lgammacor.c pbeta.c pgamma.c
  pnorm.c pt.c qchisq.c qgamma.c qnorm.c qt.c stirlerr.c toms708.c
  nmath.h dpq.h

Reduced from the headers R 4.6.2 installs (include/), keeping only what the
files above read when compiled with MATHLIB_STANDALONE:

  include/Rmath.h  include/Rconfig.h  include/R_ext/RS.h  include/R_ext/Print.h

Added for dbarts:

  prefix.h  force-included ahead of every file. It stands in for R's config.h
            (the macros the copied files read, set as R's configure sets them
            when it builds R) and renames every external symbol the copy
            defines with a dbarts_nmath_ prefix, so a program that also links
            R or a standalone libRmath sees no clash. The build fails if a
            defined symbol escapes the prefix.

Building
--------

Each .c file is compiled with

  -DMATHLIB_STANDALONE -include errno.h -include prefix.h -Iinclude

and R's own C compiler and flags (R CMD config CC, R CMD config CFLAGS); the
recipe is in tests/cpp/Makefile. Compiled that way on the reference host
(arm64 macOS, R 4.6.x) the copy returns exactly R's values: the tests/cpp
nmath suite compares the two on a grid over the six routines and their flag
combinations, bitwise there and within a relative 1e-13 elsewhere. Other
flags change the last digits (with contraction of a * b + c turned off, a
quarter of the grid moves: qnorm by up to 432 units in the last place in its
far tails, dt 50, qchisq 35, qt 11, dnorm 8), so a build that must match R's
draws compiles the copy as R compiles nmath.

Re-taking the copy
------------------

When the reference build's R moves a minor version: copy the same files from
that R's src/nmath (adding any file the closure gains; the build's link of
the standalone target names a missing one), re-reduce the four headers from
that R's installed ones, regenerate prefix.h's rename list from
"nm -g" of the compiled objects, update this file, and rerun the nmath suite.

